 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in House",
   "date": "2019-03-13",
   "text": "No Tax Breaks for Outsourcing Act \n This bill modifies the tax treatment of the foreign source income of domestic corporations. The bill includes provisions that\n eliminate an exemption for certain returns from tangible investments made overseas, \n eliminate deductions for a domestic corporation's foreign-derived intangible income and global intangible low-taxed income, \n repeal a provision that excludes foreign oil and gas extraction income from the tested income of a controlled foreign corporation, \n limit the tax deduction for the interest expenses of a U.S. corporation that is a member of a financial reporting group (i.e., a group that prepares consolidated financial statements according to generally accepted accounting principles or international financial reporting standards), \n modify the rules for the taxation of inverted corporations (U.S. corporations that acquire foreign companies to reincorporate in a foreign jurisdiction with income tax rates lower than the United States), and \n treat certain foreign corporations managed and controlled primarily in the United States as domestic corporations for tax purposes."
  }
 ],
